==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|trocken|lang=gmh}}, {{term|trucken|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|trokkan|lang=goh}}, {{term|truckan|lang=goh}}, {{term|trukkan||dried out, parched, thirsty, dry|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*druknaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*druhnaz||dry}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*dʰerǵʰ-||to strengthen; become hard or solid}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*dʰer-||to hold, hold fast, support}}. Cognate with {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|drokno||dry|pos=adverb|lang=osx}}, Old English {{m|ang|ġedrycnan||to dry up}}.

